    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hi, I am trying to modify the height of the windows in mini.files to all be the same height.\r\n\r\nIt feels like this should be doable using `MiniFilesWindowUpdate`-event. But I am unsure of how mini.files updates the height of the window. I have currently added the following snippet.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"User\", {\r\n  pattern = \"MiniFilesWindowUpdate\",\r\n  callback = function(args)\r\n    local win_id = args.data.win_id\r\n\r\n    local config = vim.api.nvim_win_get_config(win_id)\r\n    config.height = 10\r\n    vim.api.nvim_win_set_config(win_id, config)\r\n  end,\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is the behavior currently.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8fe3981d-8eb9-4044-ae1b-1b9ac8487577\r\n\r\nAs can be seen the event fires when opening the explorer, and when opening a file. Perhaps I am misunderstanding the way that the event is working? It is working as expected when settign stuff like border or winblend, is it that the plugin is setting the window height after the event has happened?\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi, I am trying to modify the height of the windows in mini.files to all be the same height.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It feels like this should be doable using <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFilesWindowUpdate</code>-event. But I am unsure of how mini.files updates the height of the window. I have currently added the following snippet.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(&quot;User&quot;, {\n  pattern = &quot;MiniFilesWindowUpdate&quot;,\n  callback = function(args)\n    local win_id = args.data.win_id\n\n    local config = vim.api.nvim_win_get_config(win_id)\n    config.height = 10\n    vim.api.nvim_win_set_config(win_id, config)\n  end,\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>User<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>MiniFilesWindowUpdate<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">win_id</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">data</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">win_id</span>\n\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">config</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_win_get_config</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">win_id</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">config</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">height</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">10</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_win_set_config</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">win_id</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">config</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is the behavior currently.</p>\n<details open=\"\" class=\"details-reset border rounded-2\">\n  <summary class=\"tmp-px-3 py-2\">\n    <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" data-component=\"Octicon\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" data-view-component=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-device-camera-video\">\n    <path d=\"M16 3.75v8.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.136.643L11 10.575v.675A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 9.25 13h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 11.25v-6.5C0 3.784.784 3 1.75 3h7.5c.966 0 1.75.784 1.75 1.75v.675l3.864-2.318A.75.75 0 0 1 16 3.75Zm-6.5 1a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25h-7.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v6.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-6.5ZM11 8.825l3.5 2.1v-5.85l-3.5 2.1Z\"></path>\n</svg>\n    <span class=\"m-1\">example_height.mp4</span>\n    <span class=\"dropdown-caret\"></span>\n  </summary>\n\n  <video src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/113891532/356995291-8fe3981d-8eb9-4044-ae1b-1b9ac8487577.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTMzOTYsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MzA5NiwicGF0aCI6Ii8xMTM4OTE1MzIvMzU2OTk1MjkxLThmZTM5ODFkLThlYjktNDA0NC1hZTFiLTFiOWFjODQ4NzU3Ny5tcDQ_.ywxqEYcW1rUg95yfqja_6s5YyAY2NGx7SeP-Dp0BKJE\" data-canonical-src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/113891532/356995291-8fe3981d-8eb9-4044-ae1b-1b9ac8487577.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTMzOTYsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MzA5NiwicGF0aCI6Ii8xMTM4OTE1MzIvMzU2OTk1MjkxLThmZTM5ODFkLThlYjktNDA0NC1hZTFiLTFiOWFjODQ4NzU3Ny5tcDQ_.ywxqEYcW1rUg95yfqja_6s5YyAY2NGx7SeP-Dp0BKJE\" controls=\"controls\" muted=\"muted\" class=\"d-block rounded-bottom-2 border-top width-fit\" style=\"max-height:640px; min-height: 200px\">\n\n  </video>\n</details>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">As can be seen the event fires when opening the explorer, and when opening a file. Perhaps I am misunderstanding the way that the event is working? It is working as expected when settign stuff like border or winblend, is it that the plugin is setting the window height after the event has happened?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hi, I am trying to modify the height of the windows in mini.files to all be the same height.\nIt feels like this should be doable using MiniFilesWindowUpdate-event. But I am unsure of how mini.files updates the height of the window. I have currently added the following snippet.\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"User\", {\n  pattern = \"MiniFilesWindowUpdate\",\n  callback = function(args)\n    local win_id = args.data.win_id\n\n    local config = vim.api.nvim_win_get_config(win_id)\n    config.height = 10\n    vim.api.nvim_win_set_config(win_id, config)\n  end,\n})\nThis is the behavior currently.\n\n  \n    \n    \n\n    example_height.mp4\n    \n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n\nAs can be seen the event fires when opening the explorer, and when opening a file. Perhaps I am misunderstanding the way that the event is working? It is working as expected when settign stuff like border or winblend, is it that the plugin is setting the window height after the event has happened?",
