            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for reporting this!\r\n\r\nYeah, I think I'd also expect setting window height to work here.\r\n\r\nThe quick test showed that the culprit is an [intentional blocking of `MiniPickWindowUpdate`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7c00ea1a6b35332746e1a2fa768e26c5fa9c3589/lua/mini/files.lua#L1846-L1848) event to reduce it getting triggered during cursor movement. Maybe having this conditioned on whether there is a preview is a better approach.\r\n\r\nThere is also a [special treatment of window height](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7c00ea1a6b35332746e1a2fa768e26c5fa9c3589/lua/mini/files.lua#L1862-L1871) that needs to be addressed for this autocommand to work. I'll take a look.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for reporting this!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Yeah, I think I'd also expect setting window height to work here.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The quick test showed that the culprit is an <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7c00ea1a6b35332746e1a2fa768e26c5fa9c3589/lua/mini/files.lua#L1846-L1848\">intentional blocking of <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPickWindowUpdate</code></a> event to reduce it getting triggered during cursor movement. Maybe having this conditioned on whether there is a preview is a better approach.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There is also a <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7c00ea1a6b35332746e1a2fa768e26c5fa9c3589/lua/mini/files.lua#L1862-L1871\">special treatment of window height</a> that needs to be addressed for this autocommand to work. I'll take a look.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Thanks for reporting this!\nYeah, I think I'd also expect setting window height to work here.\nThe quick test showed that the culprit is an intentional blocking of MiniPickWindowUpdate event to reduce it getting triggered during cursor movement. Maybe having this conditioned on whether there is a preview is a better approach.\nThere is also a special treatment of window height that needs to be addressed for this autocommand to work. I'll take a look.",
